// Bregenz/Vorarlberg.
//
// LEGAL POSITIONING NOTE — READ BEFORE EDITING:
// Austria is a CONFIDENT DUAL-TRACK market with the tightest
// compliance calendar of any country we serve. Haeuslicher Unterricht
// is a lawful way to fulfil the nine-year Schulpflicht (§ 11 Abs 2
// Schulpflichtgesetz); the education must be "mindestens
// gleichwertig" — at least equivalent — to public school. The
// mechanics, from the Bildungsdirektionen's own published guidance:
// 1. ANNUAL ANZEIGE (notification) to the Bildungsdirektion, renewed
//    EVERY school year, deadline roughly one week after the previous
//    school year ends — for 2026/27 the published deadline in several
//    Laender is Friday 17 July 2026, 12:00. The Bildungsdirektion can
//    prohibit (untersagen) participation.
// 2. MANDATORY REFLEXIONSGESPRAECH each year around the end of the
//    winter semester (Feb/March; e.g. Styria's 2025/26 deadline was
//    6 March 2026), held at the district school the child would
//    otherwise attend. It is a pedagogical orientation conversation,
//    not an exam — but NON-ATTENDANCE IS A SCHULPFLICHTVERLETZUNG and
//    the authority must order school attendance by decree.
// 3. ANNUAL EXTERNISTENPRUEFUNG between 1 JUNE and the end of the
//    school year, before a commission assigned by ordinance, covering
//    the compulsory subjects (Pflichtgegenstaende) of the school type
//    and grade — in German, with Digitale Grundbildung among the
//    subjects at relevant grades. Admission must be applied for in
//    advance; the certificate copy must be sent to the
//    Bildungsdirektion unprompted before the school year ends.
// 4. THE SANCTION IS HARD: if the exam is failed, not taken, or the
//    certificate arrives late, the Bildungsdirektion MUST order school
//    attendance for the following year ON THE GRADE NOT PASSED
//    (repeat), administrative penalty proceedings can be opened, and
//    (per Vorarlberg's guidance) a further application for haeuslicher
//    Unterricht is refused. Retaking the Externistenpruefung is not
//    permitted. There are no second chances in this framework —
//    plan accordingly and say so plainly.
// POST-15: the nine school years end around 15, but DO NOT claim a
// free window — AusBildung bis 18 (the training obligation to 18)
// applies, and how it treats an internationally educated teenager is
// a question for the AusBildung bis 18 coordination services or legal
// advice, not for our marketing. Netherlands-grade caution here.
// Smartious's model: DUAL-TRACK — the Austrian compliance calendar
// (mid-July Anzeige, Feb/March Reflexionsgespraech, 1 June exam
// window) planned beside the Cambridge calendar, with German-language
// exam preparation treated as a first-class part of the year.
// EXAM LOGISTICS NOTE: Austria's international tier is IB/American-
// dominated and CAIE provision is thin — use hedged phrasing, with
// one verified cross-reference: the International School of Brno is
// a Cambridge testing centre under two hours from Vienna.
